# Cloudflare is in front of this machine (the domain's DNS record is proxied, SSL mode "Full (strict)").
#
# Caddy believes the client address that Cloudflare passes on, and only when the request really comes from Cloudflare;
# anything else gets its own address recorded instead, so the header cannot be forged by going around Cloudflare.
# Set TRUST_PROXY_HOPS=2 for the chat-server: Caddy and Cloudflare are the two proxies in front of it.
#
# The ranges are from https://www.cloudflare.com/ips-v4 and https://www.cloudflare.com/ips-v6 (October 2026); they
# change rarely, but check them now and then.
{
	servers {
		trusted_proxies static 173.245.48.0/20 103.21.244.0/22 103.22.200.0/22 103.31.4.0/22 141.101.64.0/18 108.162.192.0/18 190.93.240.0/20 188.114.96.0/20 197.234.240.0/22 198.41.128.0/17 162.158.0.0/15 104.16.0.0/13 104.24.0.0/14 172.64.0.0/13 131.0.72.0/22 2400:cb00::/32 2606:4700::/32 2803:f800::/32 2405:b500::/32 2405:8100::/32 2a06:98c0::/29 2c0f:f248::/32
	}
}

import sites.caddy
